WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.525
Inside multiply, tile sets both shared array dimensions and the block’s two-dimensional thread shape. main derives the grid from width and tile.

00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:23.855
Zero padding handles partial tiles while every thread reaches the barriers. main verifies every output against a CPU reference on nonuniform inputs before reporting calculated loads and shared bytes; those counts alone do not identify a faster kernel.

00:00:25.355 --> 00:00:26.735
Choose tile width.

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:29.145
Set the block shape and shared arrays.

00:00:29.145 --> 00:00:30.545
Verify the product.

00:00:30.545 --> 00:00:33.670
Check correctness before comparing resources.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.215
Form a hypothesis.

00:00:35.215 --> 00:00:37.970
Measure the real GPU to test performance.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:44.005
Each resident block consumes shared storage and registers on its SM.

00:00:44.005 --> 00:00:48.225
Larger tiles can improve reuse while reducing how many blocks fit.

00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:52.785
The teaching resource budget is separate from the device-specific occupancy limits.
